  "result": "The six-question quiz on O4 is ready: `quizzes/0002.json`, with its key in `keys/0002.json`.\n\n- **What it covers:** who owns the control flow (code or model), how to classify a feature from a description, which makerspace tasks suit a fixed workflow, the cost gap when an agent takes more model calls, and which design can promise a call ceiling. The last item checks whether a step limit turns an agent into a workflow.\n- **Mix:** four multiple choice, one numeric (a cost calculation) and one one-word short answer.\n- **Ahead of the lessons:** no lesson covers O4 yet. I wrote the quiz as a check of the objective itself, from my knowledge of Anthropic's \"Building effective agents\" framing, not from a fresh source search. I can write a lesson on O4 next if you want one.\n- **New misconception ids:** I introduced M7 to M9 for this objective. M7 is classifying by tool use or call count. M8 is treating agents as always better. M9 is thinking a step limit makes an agent a workflow.\n\nI haven't changed `NOTES.md`. Quiz 0001 is still ungraded, so do you want me to grade its two submissions before you take this one?",
